{"archetypes":[{"name":"script-contract-mirror","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan collapses plan-block-write.sh to a 5-line thin wrapper and claims bit-for-bit stdout contract preservation, but that claim must be verified against the actual script, not just its documented interface.","prompt_body":"The plan rewrites `scripts/plan-block-write.sh` as a thin wrapper over `scripts/named-block-write.sh --marker plan`, asserting bit-for-bit preservation of the `WRITTEN/MODE/MARKERS_PRESENT/BODY_BYTES/MALFORMED/FAILED/ERROR` stdout contract. Read the actual current `scripts/plan-block-write.sh` and identify any behaviors — exit codes, temp-file side effects, retry sequences, error-path distinctions, or classify/redact/edit pipeline details — that are not captured by merely parameterizing the marker name. Check whether the existing block-grammar constants are truly generic over arbitrary marker names or whether any part of the script hard-codes `plan`-specific semantics that cannot be absorbed by a `--marker plan` delegation. Audit every caller of `plan-block-write.sh` under `scripts/`, `skills/`, and CI to confirm they all use only the documented CLI surface, ruling out undocumented invocation patterns that the collapse would silently break. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"step-registry-coverage","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Pause-save computes next-unfinished-step from step-sentinel files vs step-name-registry.tsv, but the plan never enumerates which SKILL.md locations gain new sentinel-write lines or whether the registry is currently complete.","prompt_body":"The pause-save mechanism computes the next unfinished step by checking `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/.completed/step-<id>` sentinels against `skills/design/scripts/step-name-registry.tsv`, yet the plan only says new sentinel-write lines are added at the top of each major step without listing specific SKILL.md locations. Read `skills/design/SKILL.md` and `skills/design/scripts/step-name-registry.tsv` side-by-side: flag any named steps present in SKILL.md that lack a registry row, and any registry rows naming steps not traceable to a SKILL.md Bash block. Identify SKILL.md step entry points whose Bash blocks reside in referenced sub-files under `skills/design/references/` rather than in the main SKILL.md, since those locations would also need the new sentinel-write line and the plan does not mention them. Verify whether the plan's assertion that `design-driver.sh --resume-from` requires no extension is consistent with how the driver currently dispatches ACTION records versus how prompt-side step routing is actually structured in SKILL.md. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"prelude-injection-audit","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan adds a pause-check line to the canonical Bash-block prelude in SKILL.md from Step 1c onward without enumerating whether the prelude is a single canonical template or per-step inline copies, leaving coverage ambiguous.","prompt_body":"The plan adds a one-line pause-check to the canonical Bash-block prelude in `skills/design/SKILL.md` from Step 1c onward, but does not enumerate the specific Bash blocks affected or state whether the prelude appears once as a shared template or is duplicated per step. Read `skills/design/SKILL.md` and count every Bash block that currently contains the env-source prelude line referencing `current-design-env-$PPID.sh`; determine whether it is a single canonical definition or per-step inline repetition. If it is a single template, confirm the plan correctly identifies exactly where that template is defined so that one edit propagates to all downstream steps automatically; if it is per-step inline, flag that the plan must enumerate and update each instance individually. Cross-check against the sub-files under `skills/design/references/` that SKILL.md includes or invokes to ensure no Bash block carrying the prelude is housed in a referenced file outside the main SKILL.md. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
